    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so as I'm traveling across southern Minnesota, you know, I'm hearing a lot of discomfort and anxiety around the inflation that we're struggling with right now in the country. You know, when people are telling me they're going to the grocery store and buying a dozen eggs for $5 or a honey crisp apple for $1.90, that is really family pocketbook issues that we just can't have happen here in this country. You look at the gas prices, what we're paying at a pump, at the pump, and how that's affecting small businesses and interrupting some supply chain decisions based on costs. So the ripple effect that has in our economy and our backyard here in Southern",
